---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { meta } from "../i18n/meta";
import { SITE_URL as siteUrl } from "../lib/site";
import { breadcrumbLd } from "../lib/breadcrumbs";
import { ogImageFor } from "../lib/og";

const m = meta.en.privacy;

const pageLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: m.title,
  description: m.description,
  inLanguage: "en",
  url: new URL("/privacy", siteUrl).toString(),
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${siteUrl}/#website` },
};
---

<Layout
  title={m.title}
  description={m.description}
  ogImage={ogImageFor("/privacy")}
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbLd("en", [
      { name: "Home", path: "/" },
      { name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy" },
    ]),
    pageLd,
  ]}
>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
      <p
        class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
      >
        Legal
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-secondary">Last updated: 2026</p>

      <div
        class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary"
      >
        <p>
          My World Cup XI is a free browser football game. This policy explains
          what data we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. It
          covers the game, the teams index, the how-to-play guide and the draft
          tool.
        </p>
        <p>
          The game runs in your browser. There is no account and no download, so
          we collect very little. By using the site you agree to this policy. If
          something is unclear, ask us on the contact page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            1. Overview
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            My World Cup XI respects your privacy. This policy covers the whole
            site: the game, the draft, the teams index and the how-to-play
            guide. It explains what we collect, how we use it, and what you can
            control.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not sell data. We do not require an account. You can open the
            game and play without giving us your name or email. If we change
            this policy, we post the update here. Where local law gives you
            stronger rights, that law applies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            2. Information we collect
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Because the game runs in your browser, most of your data stays
            there. We do not ask for your name, email or payment details to
            play. There is no sign-up and no purchase. Your draft, squad,
            formation, results and saved cups stay in your browser. They are not
            sent to our servers.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may collect basic technical data such as your IP address,
            browser, device and the pages you visit. This helps us understand
            how the game is used and fix problems. We look at grouped trends,
            not individual drafts. We do not build a profile about you.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Only routine analytics leave your device, and only if analytics is
            on. They show which features people use. You can turn them off and
            still play. Every match is calculated on your machine.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            3. Cookies and analytics
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may use cookies to remember settings and measure how the site is
            used. Analytics partners may use cookies too. They show how many
            people open the game, which formations are popular, and whether the
            teams index helps. Cookies are not required to play. The simulation
            runs on your device.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can turn off cookies at any time. The game still works. You only
            lose the anonymous signal we use to plan improvements. We do not use
            advertising cookies or run ad networks, so there is no cross-site
            tracking. Some browsers send a "Do Not Track" signal. We honour it
            where we can.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Because the game has no download, no software runs in the
            background. The only network activity is the page load and optional
            anonymous analytics. We review our cookies regularly and remove the
            ones we no longer need.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            4. How we use information
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We use the data to run and improve the site. We track down bugs,
            make the game faster, check that formations draft correctly, and
            make sure penalty shootouts work on real devices. We look at group
            trends, not single drafts. That tells us which old squads to add and
            whether the simulation feels balanced.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We do not sell or rent your data. We do not share it for
            advertising. The draft you build stays on your device. Only
            anonymous analytics reach us. We also use data to keep the service
            safe, spot unusual traffic and stop abuse. None of this requires
            knowing who you are.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If a change needs more data, we will ask first. We do not target you
            on other sites or build hidden profiles from your drafts.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            5. Data sharing
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We share data only in a few narrow cases. We may use helpers who run
            the site, such as an analytics or hosting partner. They must keep
            the data confidential and may use it only for that job. We may also
            share data if the law requires it, if we receive a valid legal
            request, or to protect the site and its users.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Your draft is stored on your device, so there is usually nothing to
            share. We never receive your tournament. The grouped analytics we
            hold may go to a measurement partner, but it is not sold and does
            not identify you. If the site changes owner, we will tell users and
            keep this policy's promises. We do not share data with advertisers,
            and the game has no ad network or cross-site tracking.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            In practice, the only sharing is the quiet help that keeps the site
            online. Your rosters and cups never leave your device.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            6. Children's privacy
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The site is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly
            collect their data. The game needs no account and no sign-up, so a
            child can play without giving us a name or email. That keeps risk
            low by design.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The content is based on World Cup history and suits fans of any age.
            We still suggest that younger players use the game with a parent. If
            a parent believes a child under 13 sent us data by email, contact us
            and we will delete it quickly. If your region sets a different age
            for consent, that age applies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            7. Your choices
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can clear your game data at any time by clearing browser storage
            for the site. That removes your drafts, squads and cups. There is no
            server copy to delete.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can also block or delete cookies, turn on Do Not Track, or use a
            privacy tool. The game still runs, and every match is calculated on
            your device. Your local law may give you more rights, such as access
            to, correction of, or deletion of data we hold. Contact us and we
            will respond within the time the law sets. We will not penalise you
            for asking.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The game is built to make these choices simple. There is no account
            to close and no download to remove.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            8. Changes to this policy
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update this policy as the game changes. We post changes on
            this page and update the "Last updated" date. If a change is
            significant, such as collecting more than anonymous analytics, we
            will say so clearly and ask first where the law requires it. Small
            changes, such as a wording fix or a new storage method, may happen
            without notice.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Check back now and then, especially if you use the teams index or
            the how-to-play guide as a reference. The main promises will not
            change: the game stays free, it sells nothing, and it keeps your
            drafts on your device. If you disagree with an update, stop using
            the site and clear your storage.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            9. Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Questions about this policy or how the game handles data? The
            contact page is the fastest way to reach us. Ask about a cookie
            setting, a data request, or a feature idea.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The game stores your drafts locally, so most deletion requests are
            solved by clearing storage. If we hold anything, such as an
            analytics choice, we will act quickly.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We welcome notes from parents, teachers and group leaders who use
            the game in class or on match day. We read every message. <a
              class="text-mint underline"
              href="/contact/">Contact us</a
            > if anything here is unclear and we will explain it plainly.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main></Layout
>
